          "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><h2>Prostate Health Index and Early Cancer Biomarker Panel</h2><p><b>Conclusion:</b> Patient has an elevated Prostate Health Index (phi = 47.8) in this synthetic test result, indicating an elevated probability of clinically significant prostate cancer (Gleason Score >= 7) on biopsy. Quantitative Immunoassay Biomarkers Biomarker / Assay LOINC Result Units Reference Range Flag Total PSA 2857-1 5.6 ng/mL 0.0 - 4.0 High (H) Free PSA 10886-0 0.58 ng/mL N/A Normal % Free PSA 19195-7 10.4 % > 25.0 % Low (L) [-2]proPSA 72304-9 19.2 pg/mL N/A Normal Prostate Health Index (phi) 72305-6 47.8 {score} < 27.0 (Low Risk) High (H)</p></div>"
